  -> expiry/restoration chain. TL006 makes no production changes.

## Historical custom-loop implementation receipt (superseded)

- `executeTargetAttempt.ts` counts Auto repeats separately from actual dispatches.
  Every eligible Auto candidate keeps its first attempt, including pools above
  200; the configured/hard cap applies to inner, whole-set, and cooldown repeats.
  Non-Auto still uses the existing total-dispatch cap.
- `comboAttemptLoop.ts` preserves Auto failure outcomes across set retries and
  omits the implicit ten-minute request timer only for Auto without a positive
  request deadline. Explicit positive deadlines, finite resolved target
  timeouts, client cancellation, and the existing Non-Auto safety timer remain.
- Auto does not stop on a three-error model streak. Existing request-global
  terminal handling remains. The uncooled same-raw-model sibling after an
  upstream 504 is covered by the Auto routing regression.
- One concise `AICODE-NOTE` marks the first-attempt/repeat policy at the target
  attempt seam. No copied upstream module, compatibility shim, new setting,
  scoring change, or public interface change was added.

