## Historical corrective continuation (before stock-test restoration)

The prior pre-existing safety-failure attribution was withdrawn based on
historical runs: clean baseline passed 51/51, and feature before fixture
correction passed 32/51. Temporary safety-fixture isolation then reported
51/51. The upstream test file was later restored; this remains diagnostic
evidence, not a current pass claim. One genuine new TS2339 in the
empty-content repeat-budget branch was addressed by narrowing before `.result`.
Baseline typecheck is 720 errors/113 files; feature was 721/114. Full comparison
remains with IND005; no full typecheck or Vitest is run in this correction.

- [x] Isolate safety fixture and restore 51/51 without changing Non-Auto policy.
- [x] Add meaningful empty-content/repeat-budget RED cases, fix union branch,
      and verify later success plus complete all-failure aggregate.
- [x] Run lifetime, affected routing batch, 499, safety, scoped lint/format,
      Code Simplifier review, and strict package validation.

### Corrective RED and GREEN evidence

Before the production correction, the lifetime/attempt/safety command ran
102 tests: 101 passed and one failed. The new target-runner assertion
`exhausted empty-content retry must return the normal failed-target outcome`
observed `undefined` instead of `null` (`/tmp/ex002-corrective-red.log`). The
public empty-content cases already reached later success and preserved aggregate
identities/errors; the direct assertion exposes the invalid union branch.

`handleEmptyContentRetry` records last error/status, `comboErrors` with
`empty_content`, recorded attempts, and failure trust before returning its
retry decision. Exhausted repeat budget now returns `null` without overwriting
that state; a permitted repeat continues, and `.result` is accessed only on the
non-retry union member. The direct regression verifies the recorded error,
status, model, actual dispatch count, and unchanged exhausted repeat count.

Focused lifetime tests also now assert actual scored first-pass order for
whole-set repeats instead of assuming input order among equally scored models.
The identical-error fixture emits three model-classified failures before the
fourth distinct dispatch succeeds, regardless of scored tie order. The 32/max30
and >200 winner-by-model-identity regressions remain intact.

Code Simplifier reviewed this corrective production branch: explicit narrowing,
one budget check, and `return null` are sufficient. No cast, new abstraction,
journal, scheduler, production Non-Auto change, or cooldown/bridge change.

Corrective RED command:
`node --import tsx/esm --import ./open-sse/utils/setupPolyfill.ts --import ./tests/_setup/isolateDataDir.ts --test --test-force-exit --test-concurrency=1 tests/unit/auto-fallback-request-lifetime.test.ts tests/unit/combo/execute-target-attempt.test.ts tests/unit/combo-safety-stop.test.ts`.
The GREEN commands are the four exact Node commands in Verification above;
results are 19/19, 84/84, 7/7, and 51/51 (161 passing tests total). Logs:
`/tmp/ex002-corrective-lifetime.log`, `/tmp/ex002-corrective-batch.log`,
`/tmp/ex002-corrective-499.log`, `/tmp/ex002-corrective-safety.log`.

